  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Sikorsky Aircraft has $2.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Sikorsky Aircraft won 9,857 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $285K. Obligations fell 41.9% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a peak at $5.3B in FY23 and a decline to $2.8B in FY26, after $4.8B in both FY24 and FY25, $3.4B in FY22, and $4.9B in FY21. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $2.7B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $61.9M and the Department of Justice with $8.2M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sikorsky Aircraft at $2.5B, with Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $248M and a range of smaller markets from Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $19.8M to Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $167K.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2026 obligations total $2.8B, below the FY23 peak of $5.3B. FY2026 follows two consecutive fiscal years at $4.8B and a FY22 total of $3.4B and a FY21 total of $4.9B. Obligations fell 41.9% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Sikorsky Aircraft's main buyers and what markets do they buy in?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $2.7B from Sikorsky Aircraft in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $61.9M and the Department of Justice obligated $8.2M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market at $2.5B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $248M and several smaller markets including Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $19.8M and Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $18.3M."
      }
    ]
